If a patient has a prescribed-opioid and has a prescribed-opioid-nonuse and a repeated-negative-test-series verifies the prescribed-opioid-nonuse and a confirmatory-test verifies the prescribed-opioid-nonuse then every clinician may discontinue the prescribed-opioid and may discuss a safe-unused-opioid-disposal-option with the patient.
If a patient has a prescribed-opioid and has a prescribed-opioid-nonuse and a repeated-negative-test-series verifies the prescribed-opioid-nonuse and a confirmatory-test verifies the prescribed-opioid-nonuse then the patient does not require an opioid-taper.
